# ── cart/editor/data: game models. The whole directory is ignored ────────────
# USER RULING (req_3772 follow-up): "that directory is to be ignored". Every
# asset the editor writes here — models/, textures/, stickers/, and whatever
# asset dir it grows next — never reaches GitHub, with no rule to remember.
#
# The `*` + re-include form is deliberate. Ignoring `cart/editor/data/` outright
# makes git skip the directory without descending, so nothing inside can ever be
# re-included — and this directory is ALSO the editor's source tree (73 .ts
# files: commands, types, meshDoc, the stores). Those stayed tracked only
# because git keeps tracking what it already tracks; every NEW source file added
# here was silently invisible to git. Ignoring the directory's CONTENTS and
# exempting source keeps both halves of the ruling true.
/cart/editor/data/*
!/cart/editor/data/*.ts

# The user's personal image-generation console (embedded API key) — never git's.
